    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0345" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.5064P19/9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-25T12:00:00-06:00">March 25,
                        1929—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>29. With reference to Department’s instruction No. 500, September 13,
                        1922,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d235-f1"/> Legation is informed that the Honduran
                    Government is again demanding deposit of $50,000 from Pan American Life
                    Insurance Company under decree 107, April 1, 1922. I shall take the matter <pb
                        facs="0346" n="228" xml:id="pg228"/> up informally today but I request
                    instructions to enter formal protest along the lines of the Department’s No.
                    328, February 4th last.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
